# ⚠️ NO LONGER USED BY builder/Dockerfile, and kept only so a stray root-context
# build does not ship the repo.
#
# It used to matter: the builder image was built with the REPO ROOT as its
# context, and this trimmed that to builder/ and runtime/ so ~500 MB of
# third_party/elfconv did not cross the wire.
#
# Since 2026-08-23 the context is `builder/_stage` — the ~20 MB tree
# //builder:stage produces, which is exactly the files the image gains and
# nothing else. A context that IS the payload needs no ignore file.
#
# `raptormark build-image` passes that directory explicitly. If you find
# yourself running `docker build -f builder/Dockerfile .` by hand, that is the
# mistake this file now guards: the Dockerfile is `COPY . /`, so a root context
# would copy the repository into the image.
*
!builder
!runtime
